  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n## Description\nThe `PauserRegistry::deauthorizeContract` function removes a contract from the list of authorized contracts but fails to automatically pause it. This oversight allows deauthorized contracts to remain fully operational, even though they should no longer be accessible.\n\nWhile the system includes a separate pause function, it can only be called on authorized contracts. This creates a logical gap: once a contract is deauthorized, it cannot be paused, leaving the protocol exposed to unintended interactions.\nDeauthorization of a contract should also pause a contract \n## Impact \n- Unauthorized Access: Deauthorized contracts remain active, allowing users to interact with them despite their revoked permissions.\n- Financial Risk: If a contract is deauthorized due to security concerns (e.g., a compromised StakingManager), users could still deposit funds, leading to potential losses.\n  \n## Example \n1.The StakingManager is initially authorized for staking operations.\n2.Due to a discovered vulnerability (e.g., reward calculation flaw), it is deauthorized via deauthorizeContract.\n3.However, since the contract is not automatically paused, users continue depositing funds, exposing them to exploitation\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nModify `PauserRegistry::deauthorizeContract` to force-pause the contract upon deauthorization. This ensures no interactions are possible after access is revoked\n```diff\nfunction deauthorizeContract(address contractAddress) external onlyRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE) {\n        require(_authorizedContracts.contains(contractAddress), \"Contract not authorized\");\n+if(!isPaused[contractAddress]) {\n+            isPaused[contractAddress] = true;\n+        }\n        _authorizedContracts.remove(contractAddress);\n        emit ContractDeauthorized(contractAddress);\n    }\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Code \nAdd the following test case to `PauserRegistry.t.sol`\n```solidity \n function test_DeauthorizedContract_RemainsUnpaused_AllowingDangerousInteractions() public {\n    // Setup: Simulate a contract address to be authorized\n    address mockContract = makeAddr(\"MockContract\");\n\n    // Start admin transaction\n    vm.startPrank(admin);\n\n    // 1. Authorize the contract and verify it's authorized but unpaused\n    pauserRegistry.authorizeContract(mockContract);\n    assertTrue(pauserRegistry.isAuthorizedContract(mockContract), \"Contract should be authorized\");\n    assertFalse(pauserRegistry.isPaused(mockContract), \"Contract should NOT be paused after authorization\");\n\n    // 2. Deauthorize the contract (critical security action)\n    pauserRegistry.deauthorizeContract(mockContract);\n\n    // 3. Verify the contract is deauthorized but STILL unpaused (BUG)\n    assertFalse(pauserRegistry.isAuthorizedContract(mockContract), \"Contract should be deauthorized\");\n    assertFalse(pauserRegistry.isPaused(mockContract), \"BUG: Deauthorized contract remains unpaused\");\n\n    vm.stopPrank();\n\n    // 4. (Optional) Simulate a user interacting with the deauthorized-but-unpaused contract\n    vm.deal(user, 1 ether); // Give user some ether for the interaction\n    vm.prank(user);\n    (bool success, ) = mockContract.call{value: 1 ether}(abi.encodeWithSignature(\"stake()\"));\n    assertTrue(success, \"User can still interact with deauthorized contract\"); // This should FAIL in a secure system\n}\n```",
